description:
All pure, all unit-tested, no React. New files under `applications/openthrottle-developer/app/routing/settings/repositories/`:

**`config/repositories.defaults.ts`** — `REPOSITORIES_DEFAULT_LIMIT`, plus `REPOSITORIES_SORT_BY` / `REPOSITORIES_SORT_ORDER` as `as const` arrays with derived types (mirror `~/routing/projects/config`, and `ProjectsToolbar`'s use of `PROJECTS_SORT_BY`). No enums.

**`data/types.ts`** — the row type. One row = one checkout, carrying its parent repository context:
```
interface RepositoryCheckoutRow {
  branch: string | null;
  checkout: RepositoryCheckoutFieldsFragment;
  children?: RepositoryCheckoutRow[];
  isWorktree: boolean;
  repositoryId: string;
  repositoryName: string;
  remoteUrl: string | null;
}
```

**`utils/rows.ts`** — `buildRepositoryRows(repositories)`: for each repository, the `kind === 'primary'` checkout becomes the parent and `kind === 'worktree'` checkouts become `children`. Handle the real-world edge cases explicitly and test each: a repository with zero checkouts (skip, or emit a parent-less placeholder — decide and document), a repository with several `primary` checkouts (each becomes its own parent row), and worktrees with no primary sibling (promote the first to parent rather than dropping it). Branch resolves as `checkout.inspection?.git.currentBranch ?? repository.defaultBranch ?? null`.

**`utils/search.ts`** — `filterRepositoryRows(rows, search)`: case-insensitive match over repository name, `displayName`, `filesystemPath`, `normalizedRemoteUrl`, and branch. A child match retains the parent; a parent match retains all children. Also return the set of parent row ids that matched only via a child, so the table can auto-expand them.

**`utils/sorting.ts`** — `sortRepositoryRows(rows, sortBy, sortOrder)` over name / updatedAt / checkout count. Children sort within their parent only.

**Done when:** `__tests__` cover every branch above (including the three grouping edge cases and child-match-pulls-parent), and `:lint` / `:typecheck` / `:test` are green for `openthrottle-developer`.

