Add `GlobalPopover` to `packages/react-router-ui-global`.

**Read the reference first**: `applications/openthrottle-developer/app/routing/settings/repositories/components/RepositoryRowActions.tsx` (the `/settings/repositories` route). That file is the model — the API below is a generalization of what it already does, and the thinner queues menu (`routing/queues/data/queues-table-columns.tsx`) must fit inside the same API.

Scaffold — do not hand-write the file:

```bash
NX_ISOLATE_PLUGINS=false pnpm nx g @tools/generators:react-router --subGenerator=component --describe
```

use the sub-generator that targets a package (confirm exact flags with `--describe`; `--folder` takes the full path, e.g. `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/components`).

**Implementation**

- Build on the shadcn `DropdownMenu` family re-exported from `@openthrottle/react-router-shadcn` (`DropdownMenu`, `DropdownMenuTrigger`, `DropdownMenuContent`, `DropdownMenuLabel`, `DropdownMenuSeparator`, `DropdownMenuItem`) plus `AlertDialog*` for the confirm path — see the plan description for why this is a DropdownMenu despite the name.
- Default trigger: a `ghost` `size="icon"` `Button` (`className="size-7"`) with `MoreHorizontalIcon` (`size-4`, `aria-hidden`) and a required `aria-label`, matching `RepositoryRowActions` today. Allow a `trigger` override slot.
- `align` defaults to `'end'`; the wrapper is `flex justify-end`.

**Props (target shape — adjust names only if lint/type reality forces it)**

```ts
export type GlobalPopoverAction =
  | { confirm?: GlobalPopoverConfirm; destructive?: boolean; disabled?: boolean; fields: Record<string, string>; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'submit'; label: string; method?: 'post'; pending?: boolean; pendingLabel?: string; separatorBefore?: boolean }
  | { disabled?: boolean; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'link'; label: string; separatorBefore?: boolean; to: string }
  | { disabled?: boolean; icon?: React.ReactNode; id: string; kind: 'select'; label: string; onSelect: () => void; separatorBefore?: boolean };

export interface GlobalPopoverConfirm {
  cancelLabel?: string;
  confirmLabel?: string;
  description: React.ReactNode;
  title: string;
}

export interface GlobalPopoverProps {
  actions: GlobalPopoverAction[];
  align?: 'center' | 'end' | 'start';
  ariaLabel: string;
  className?: string;
  heading?: string;
  testId?: string;
  trigger?: React.ReactNode;
}
```

- `kind: 'submit'` renders a `Form method="post"` with hidden inputs from `fields` and a submit `button` inside `DropdownMenuItem asChild` — exactly the pattern in `RepositoryRowActions`. `pending: true` disables the item and shows `pendingLabel`; callers derive it from `useNavigation` (keep the derivation at the call site, it's row-specific).
- `confirm` routes the item through `AlertDialog` — the item's `onSelect` calls `event.preventDefault()` and opens the dialog; the actual `Form` submit lives in `AlertDialogAction`. `description` is a `React.ReactNode` so callers can emphasize a name inline.
- `kind: 'link'` renders `DropdownMenuItem asChild` around a `react-router` `Link` with `viewTransition`.
- `kind: 'select'` calls `onSelect`.
- `destructive: true` applies `text-destructive`; `separatorBefore` emits a `DropdownMenuSeparator`.

**Boundaries**

- Discriminated union per `.agents/rules/coding/discriminated-unions.mdc`; no enums, no `as` casts, explicit return types, `import type` for types.
- Component file exports only `GlobalPopover`, `GlobalPopoverProps`, and the closely-related action/confirm types. Default copy (fallback confirm labels, `Actions` header text) goes in `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/data/data.copy.ts`.
- Keep the six section markers and the 210-line cap — the confirm wrapper will likely need to be its own sibling component file (one component per file).
- Export from `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/index.ts`, alphabetized with the other `./components/Global*` exports. Tag package public API exports with JSDoc `@public` so Knip keeps them.

**Also add** the canonical actions-column header so tables stop hand-rolling it: a `GLOBAL_POPOVER_COPY.actionsHeader` constant (`'Actions'`) and a right-aligned header renderer matching the current queues markup — `<div className="py-2 text-right"><span className="text-sm font-medium">Actions</span></div>` — in its own file if it needs to be a component.

**Tests** — `packages/react-router-ui-global/src/components/__tests__/GlobalPopover.test.tsx`, using `component` (not `screen`) and `userEvent` (not `fireEvent`), inside a `createRoutesStub`/memory router so `Link` and `Form` resolve. Cover: trigger opens the menu; each of the three action kinds renders and fires; `pending` shows `pendingLabel` and blocks activation; `disabled` blocks activation; `separatorBefore` renders a separator; a `confirm` action opens the dialog and only submits after confirming (and not on cancel).

**Validate**

```bash
pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:lint && pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:typecheck && pnpm nx run @openthrottle/react-router-ui-global:test
```

plus `pnpm run audit:component-shape`. Run targets sequentially, never `--parallel`.

In `packages/nestjs-repositories/src/modules/skill-usage-events/skill-usage-events.service.ts` add a `searchGitBranches` method plus its result types.

Shape:

```ts
export interface SkillUsageGitBranchRow {
  readonly branch: string;
  readonly count: number;
}

export interface SkillUsageGitBranchSearchResult {
  readonly hasMore: boolean;
  readonly items: readonly SkillUsageGitBranchRow[];
}

searchGitBranches(query: {
  readonly end: string;
  readonly limit?: number | null;
  readonly query?: string | null;
  readonly skillName?: string | null;
  readonly start: string;
}): Promise<SkillUsageGitBranchSearchResult>
```

Implementation notes:
- Build on the existing `dateRangeQuery` helper (half-open `[start, endExclusive)`) and the same `skillName` narrowing `listFilterOptions` uses.
- `git_branch IS NOT NULL AND git_branch <> ''`, `GROUP BY e.git_branch`, `addSelect('COUNT(*)', 'count')`.
- Search: trim the incoming query; when non-empty add `e.git_branch ILIKE :pattern` with a parameterized `%…%`. Escape `%`, `_`, and `\` in the user input first (small exported `escapeLikePattern` util with its own test) so a branch named `feat/100%_done` can't wildcard.
- Ordering in SQL: `.orderBy('(e.git_branch <> :defaultBranch)', 'ASC').addOrderBy('e.git_branch', 'ASC')` with `defaultBranch = 'main'`. Postgres sorts `false` before `true`, so `main` lands first and everything else is A–Z. Define `SKILL_USAGE_DEFAULT_BRANCHES = ['main', 'master'] as const` and pin whichever is present (main wins when both are).
- `limit`: default 20, clamp to `[1, 50]`. Fetch `limit + 1` rows to compute `hasMore`, then slice back to `limit`.

Also cap `listFilterOptions` (both branches and cwds) at 50 so the legacy field can't return an unbounded array.

Tests in `skill-usage-events.service.test.ts`: default ordering puts `main` first then alphabetical; a `master`-only dataset pins `master`; ILIKE is case-insensitive and substring-matching; LIKE metacharacters are escaped, not honored; `limit` clamps and `hasMore` flips correctly; `skillName` narrows; empty range returns `{ hasMore: false, items: [] }`.
